    <string name="about_title">About Songlass</string>
    <string name="about_tagline">Your local music player.</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_title">Your music, your device</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_body">Your library, playlists, favourites and history stay on your device and, on Android, out of automatic backups. Audio files are never sent. Manual backups are not encrypted and go wherever you choose, including a cloud service.</string>
    <string name="about_lyrics_title">Online lyrics</string>
    <string name="about_lyrics_body">When you open Lyrics without local lyrics, Songlass sends title, artist and album to AMLL (if on) and to LRCLIB, which also gets the duration. Both see your IP address, never your audio. You can turn AMLL off in Settings → Lyrics.</string>
    <string name="about_lyrics_source">AMLL TTML Database</string>
    <string name="about_tags_title">Editing your files</string>
    <string name="about_tags_body">The tag editor changes the selected audio file. If saving is interrupted, recovery copies stay on the device: you can export them, then close the recovery, which does not repair the file.</string>

